Z||000003||Spektyr||05-13-2001||06:25 PM||||Swap it for a FWD motor that some guy with a RWD doesn't want?<P>Sell it for money to buy a FWD motor?  I'm no expert, but from what I've read here putting a RWD motor in a Fiero is not the sort of thing anyone does twice.  (In other words, if they've done it once they don't ever want to do it again.)<P>Then again, there's Fieros out there with Big block 8's mounted longitudinally, so where there's a will there's a way.  Me personally, I wouldn't want to go to that much trouble for a ho-hum motor.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||05-13-2001||06:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektyr:<BR><B>Swap it for a FWD motor that some guy with a RWD doesn't want?<P>Sell it for money to buy a FWD motor?  I'm no expert, but from what I've read here putting a RWD motor in a Fiero is not the sort of thing anyone does twice.  (In other words, if they've done it once they don't ever want to do it again.)<P>Then again, there's Fieros out there with Big block 8's mounted longitudinally, so where there's a will there's a way.  Me personally, I wouldn't want to go to that much trouble for a ho-hum motor.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Except for the popular 3.4 converstions that use the F-body RWD engine - but I digress.  Anyway, what you have there is a 3.8V6, not a 3800 V6.  They're two different engines.  You don't want to do it.  Sell it and buy a 3800.  Plus that old of a 3.8 would probably only have about as much HP as a stock 2.8, maybe a 3.1.  You'd be wasting you time, effort, and money, IMO.||||reg||13
